       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for inpatients is 3,200 mg/day. That is double the limit, and it raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, which is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses, such as 400 mg 4 times daily.\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. Tell me the clinical reason too, and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
